::: outcomes
- Derive the eigenvalue method for $\X'=\A\X$.
- Solve systems with distinct real eigenvalues, including IVPs.
- Solve systems with a repeated eigenvalue having a full set of eigenvectors.
- Use the theorem on real symmetric matrices.
:::

::: timeplan
0-15  | The method $\X=\K e^{\lambda t}$
15-30 | Distinct real eigenvalues; @ex:saddle
30-45 | A $3\times3$ IVP; @ex:ivp
45-60 | Repeated eigenvalues, Case I; @ex:case1
60-72 | Symmetric matrices; @ex:sym
72-75 | Summary and MCQs
